 "text": "Hi! How's everything today? A sketch is a fast, simple drawing done in a short amount of time, usually just for fun. A study, on the other hand, is a more detailed and realistic drawing of one subject. Yeah, it's like when you have to draw a really specific object, like a tree or a face. You take your time and pay attention to the details. Great! You'll want start with a quick sketch just to get the shape. That's good starting point. Then go back and study each cloud separately, filling in the detail. The shape, the light, and the texture. That's a fun sketch to do in one sitting. Good luck!",
